'''''Kalanchoe porphyrocalyx''''' is a species of ''[[Kalanchoe]]'' native to [[Madagascar]].<ref>{{Cite web|title=''Kalanchoe porphyrocalyx'' (Baker) Baill.|url=http://powo.science.kew.org/taxon/urn:lsid:ipni.org:names:274441-1|access-date=2020-09-17|author=|date=|format=|work=Plants of the World Online|publisher=Kew Science|language=en}}</ref>

Many [[cultivar]]s have been derived from ''K. porphyrocalyx''. 'Wendy' is a multiflorous cultivar with 15–30 flowers in an [[inflorescence]], which may derive solely from ''K. porphyrocalyx''<ref>{{Cite journal |last=Smith |first=Gideon F. |last2=Shtein |first2=Ronen |date=2021-01-06 |title=Taxonomic notes on ''Kalanchoe porphyrocalyx'' (Crassulaceae subfam. Kalanchooideae) and its horticultural derivatives |url=https://www.biotaxa.org/Phytotaxa/article/view/phytotaxa.478.2.4 |journal=Phytotaxa |volume=478 |issue=2 |pages=225–238 |doi=10.11646/phytotaxa.478.2.4 |issn=1179-3163|url-access=subscription }}</ref> or originate from hybridization between ''[[Kalanchoe miniata|K. miniata]]'' and ''K. porphyrocalyx''.<ref>{{Cite book|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=n2fHDGuqz6wC&pg=PA30|last3=Cubey|pages=|location=Cambridge, UK|year=|title=The European Garden Flora Flowering Plants: A Manual for the Identification of Plants Cultivated in Europe, Both Out-of-Doors and Under Glass|last4=Shaw|first4=J. M. H.|first3=H. Suzanne|publisher=Cambridge University Press|last2=Knees|first2=Sabina G.|last=Cullen|first=James|language=en|isbn=978-0-521-76155-0|date=2011-08-11|page=30}}</ref>

